A||||8||rc5star||Is this safe to do?||||1||
Z||000000||rc5star||07-23-2001||08:29 AM||||Would it damage the valves if I take a grinder to the heads to make them match up better with the intake? The heads are in but the intake is still out. ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Ken Wittlief||07-23-2001||09:13 AM||||what exactly do you mean by match up better?!<P> if your intake plenium doesnt match up with your heads then something is wrong with the way the engine is assembled.||||reg||11
Z||000002||rc5star||07-23-2001||09:31 AM||||The intake fit on fine but if you look down the intake into the head you can see that the air would not flow smooth becasue the head air intake is a bit smaller than the intake. That is the best way I can discribe it. It looks like the air would hit this small rigdge instead of flowing in smooth. I just didnt know if the dust from grinding would damage anything.||||reg||1
Z||000003||skitime||07-23-2001||09:44 AM||||You would only want to do that if the heads were off the block.||||reg||1
Z||000004||rogergarrison||07-23-2001||11:45 AM||||what skitime says. If you do it on the car all the fine metal bits will get on valve seats, cyl walls and eventually all the bearing. wont be long till you have cpl hundred pounds of scrap metal. You can do it if you want with the heads off.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Carrolles||07-23-2001||12:39 PM||||If you are not able to remove the heads to do the Gasket Match porting (grind the ports in the head and intake to match the opening in the gasket) at least do this to the three parts of the intake manifold.  You'll get some free HP.||||reg||1
Z||000006||StuGood||07-23-2001||04:23 PM||||Hmmm.  I don't know - I might be willing to try it, but with some big <B>if's</B>:<P>1) <B>If</B> I felt like there was some significant mismatch between manifold and head ports.  I'd have to convince myself that it'd be worth taking the following precautions... <P>2) <B>If</B> I loosened the rocker arms, to ensure the intake valves stayed shut, during the grinding process.<P>3) <B>If</B> I could plug the intake port with paper and Form-A-Gasket (or something) to keep stuff from going down too far into the intake port.<P>4) <B>If</B> I masked off the rest of the engine to keep grindin's from falling onto the cam, into crankcase, etc.<P>5) <B>If</B> I ran a shop vac while grinding, to capture stuff as it was generated, and carefully cleaned up with shop vac + magnet after doing each port.<P>6) <B>If</B> I repeated the above for all six intake ports...     <P>It would be pretty tedious, I bet (no, I've never tried it).  By the time I went to all that trouble, I'd probably wish I would have just ported the manifold sections (as Carrolles said), or just pulled the head off (as everyone else says).  Just my opinion... ||||reg||7
Z||000007||West Coast Fiero||07-23-2001||04:53 PM||||about as safe as a smoker in a FIREWORKS wharehouse<P>BOOM||||reg||1
Z||000008||skitime||07-23-2001||06:45 PM||||I would say about a likely as burying yourself naked in the sand and getting no sand in you crack.  ||||reg||1
